      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Many unused imports\n- An unused `data_invalid()` helper method\n- A vague variable name `test5`\n- No comments explaining the intent of boundary-value cases\n\nI'll write a cleaned-up version now.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and the unused `data_invalid()` method, renames `test5` to the more descriptive `fiveYears`, and adds brief inline comments that explain the intent of each assertion (including why the boundary cases use `MAX_VALUE - 1` and `MIN_VALUE + 1`)."
